---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Divisions" description="Directory of Mathim Divisions initiatives: research, systems practice, writing, and independent creative work.">
  <section class="interior-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="signal"></span>Directory / Areas of operation</p>
      <h1>Different work.<br /><em>Shared intent.</em></h1>
      <p>Mathim is a structure for whatever deserves to exist. These are the areas currently in motion.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="editorial-section" id="research">
    <div class="container editorial-columns">
      <p class="editorial-kicker">Division 01 / Research</p>
      <div class="editorial-copy">
        <h2>Research &<br />development.</h2>
        <p>The Smol Model Company of New Haven is an independent research lab investigating useful model capability under constraints of compute, memory, bandwidth, latency, energy, data, and deployment.</p>
        <p>Its work emphasizes controlled experiments and evidence rather than performance theater. The lab is an affiliated initiative with its own research identity and public site.</p>
        <a class="arrow-link" href="https://thesmolmodel.co" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit The Smol Model Company <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="editorial-section alt" id="systems">
    <div class="container editorial-columns">
      <p class="editorial-kicker">Division 02 / Systems</p>
      <div class="editorial-copy">
        <h2>Systems &<br />technical practice.</h2>
        <p>Practical IT work: audits, documentation, standard operating procedures, and technical roadmaps. The aim is simple: make complex environments understandable and leave the people who operate them with something useful.</p>
        <p>The original Mathim IT offerings remain here, rather than becoming the identity of the whole organization.</p>
        <div class="service-pricing">
          <div class="pricing-card"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Technical</p><h3>Focused Audit</h3><p>A review of one environment area, with findings and recommendations.</p><span class="price">Starting at $300</span></div>
          <div class="pricing-card"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Technical</p><h3>Full Environment Audit</h3><p>Systems, devices, security and backups, with a prioritized roadmap.</p><span class="price">Starting at $1,200</span></div>
          <div class="pricing-card"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Technical</p><h3>Readiness Review</h3><p>Gap analysis and practical documentation for a specified framework.</p><span class="price">Starting at $2,500</span></div>
        </div>
        <p>Documentation, SOPs, and strategy work are also available by discussion. Each engagement is scoped individually.</p>
        <a class="arrow-link" href="/contact">Discuss a project <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="editorial-section" id="publications">
    <div class="container editorial-columns">
      <p class="editorial-kicker">Division 03 / Publications</p>
      <div class="editorial-copy">
        <h2>Writing, tools<br />& other work.</h2>
        <p>Essays, documentation kits, prototypes, and other work that benefits from a home but not a fixed definition. The original project showcase lives on here, without having to carry the entire corporate identity.</p>
        <div class="index-table">
          <div class="index-line"><span class="index">01</span><div><h3>The Vesper Blog</h3><p>Writing about technology, continuity, and practice.</p></div><a href="https://acgh213.github.io/vesper-blog/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read ↗</a></div>
          <div class="index-line"><span class="index">02</span><div><h3>Tools & documentation</h3><p>Downloadable resources and practical templates.</p></div><a href="https://mathim.gumroad.com/l/epwnh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore ↗</a></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>